{{!--
The <source> of the collection banner (home/row-banner.hbs) from 64rem on, where the banner is a strip (372 px high,
942 to 1328 px wide: about 3.6 times wider than high). A 16:9 picture covering it would show half of its height and
download twice what is seen. Ghost crops the picture itself, from its centre as the banner's object-fit: cover does:
theme image_sizes "banner" (1400 x 392) and "banner-xl" (2000 x 560). Covering the strip takes a picture whose width
is 3.6 times its height, that is 1328 px at 1x whatever the width of the screen (a narrower banner is as high),
hence sizes="1328px": 1x takes the first, any higher density the second. An SVG keeps its own format (see
image/srcset.hbs).
Parameters: image=... the banner's picture
--}}
{{~#match image "~$" ".svg"~}}
  <source media="(min-width: 64rem)" srcset="{{img_url image size="banner"}} 1400w, {{img_url image size="banner-xl"}} 2000w" sizes="1328px">
{{~else match image "~$" ".SVG"~}}
  <source media="(min-width: 64rem)" srcset="{{img_url image size="banner"}} 1400w, {{img_url image size="banner-xl"}} 2000w" sizes="1328px">
{{~else~}}
  <source media="(min-width: 64rem)" srcset="{{img_url image size="banner" format="webp"}} 1400w, {{img_url image size="banner-xl" format="webp"}} 2000w" sizes="1328px">
{{~/match~}}
